    <string name="font_axes_info_title">Parameter axes (glyph shape)</string>
    <string name="font_axes_info_ok">Got it</string>
    <string name="font_axes_info_message"><![CDATA[<b>Standard axes</b><br/><br/>
• <b>Width (wdth)</b> — Width: condensed ↔ expanded (flatter or wider sides).<br/><br/>
• <b>Weight (wght)</b> — Weight: Light → Regular → Bold → Black.<br/><br/>
• <b>Optical Size (opsz)</b> — Optimizes drawing for small (UI) or large (titles) sizes.<br/><br/>
• <b>Grade (GRAD)</b> — Visual weight without changing advance width: denser or lighter while keeping layout.<br/><br/>
• <b>Slant (slnt)</b> — Oblique slant (not a true italic).<br/><br/>
<b>Parametric axes (glyph shape)</b><br/><br/>
• <b>Thick stroke (XOPQ)</b> — Thickness of vertical strokes (stems of H, I, n…).<br/><br/>
• <b>Thin stroke (YOPQ)</b> — Thickness of horizontal strokes (bars of E, H, f…).<br/><br/>
• <b>Counter width (XTRA)</b> — Counter width (inner gaps): tighter or more open.<br/><br/>
• <b>Uppercase (YTUC)</b> — Cap height.<br/><br/>
• <b>Lowercase (YTLC)</b> — x-height.<br/><br/>
• <b>Ascender (YTAS)</b> — Ascender height (b, d, h, l…).<br/><br/>
• <b>Descender (YTDE)</b> — Descender depth (g, p, q, y…).<br/><br/>
• <b>Figure height (YTFI)</b> — Figure height / proportion (very useful for clocks).<br/><br/>
<i>Note:</i> All these variations are available in full variable fonts such as Roboto Flex. On fixed fonts or fonts with fewer axes, unsupported controls are ignored.]]></string>
